course: dictionary
lesson: 15480
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. «She felt stressed before her spelling test.» Here stressed means worried and tense, as if you are under pressure.
explain: «Say PEN-cil: the stress falls on PEN.» In a word with more than one syllable, the stressed syllable is said more strongly than the others. Listen for it when you read aloud, and it will help you say the word the right way.
explain: «The coach stressed that everyone must wear a helmet.» Here stressed is the past of the verb stress, and it means said that something was very important. Ask yourself: what does the writer want me to understand? Then try the meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Stressed can mean feeling worried, tense and under pressure.
fact: In a word, the stressed syllable is the one said more strongly, like PEN in «pencil».
fact: «Stressed the importance of» means said that something was very important.
fact: Stressed can also describe a material under force or pressure, like a «stressed beam».
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning: look at the words around the word.
exercise: «After the loud alarm, Sam felt stressed and his tummy hurt.» What does stressed mean here? | *Worried and tense | Happy and relaxed | Bored of school | Very clean
exercise: Which syllable of «pencil» is stressed? | Neither is said strongly | Both are said equally strongly | *PEN | cil
exercise: «The coach stressed that everyone must wear a helmet.» What does stressed mean? | Forgot all about it | *Said it was very important | Felt sad about it | Broke into small pieces
test: «Ben was stressed about his maths test, so he talked to his teacher.» What does stressed mean? | Asleep | *Under pressure and worried | Very cold | Excited for a party
test: «The engineer checked the stressed beam before the bridge opened.» What does stressed mean here? | Made of soft wool | Said very quietly | Painted bright red | *Under force or pressure
exam: «When you feel stressed, take a slow breath and break your work into small steps.» Which is a good way to cope with stress? | Shout at everyone around you | *Breathe slowly and take one small step | Skip your lessons for a week | Stay up all night worrying
